# Streaming refactor #11 chunk 6 peak-RSS bench meta
date: 2026-05-18
commit: chunk-6-WIP (chunk 4 reapplied + chunk 6 Buffering dispatch + WritableSeek)
host: $(hostname)
example_default: jxl-encoder/examples/bench_buffering_rss.rs (default LossyConfig::encode())
example_rate_control: jxl-encoder/examples/bench_buffering_rss_rate_control.rs (VarDctEncoder::encode_with_rate_control_config)
build: cargo build --release -p jxl-encoder [--features rate-control for the rate-control bench]
measurement: /usr/bin/time -v "Maximum resident set size (kbytes)"

# Key findings:
# 1. Default LossyConfig::encode() path: identical peak RSS (881-883 MB) and
#    identical bytes (6973041) across all 5 Buffering variants. This is the
#    backwards-compat guarantee — the default path goes through encoder.rs:
#    encode_inner which does inline precompute and never hits the chunk-6
#    dispatch in EncoderPrecomputed::compute_with_budget_and_buffering.
#
# 2. Rate-control path: peak RSS DIVERGES by Buffering variant:
#    - FullBuffered:   2504 MiB, bytes=4131213 (whole-image precompute)
#    - Threshold2048:  2579 MiB, bytes=4131213 (also whole-image; chunk 6 routes
#                                                Threshold2048 to whole-image)
#    - Auto:           2651 MiB, bytes=4133123 (Auto resolves to BufferedOutput
#                                                at 3072² > 2048², engages per-region)
#    - BufferedOutput: 2811 MiB, bytes=4133123 (per-region; +12% RSS vs FullBuffered)
#    - FullStreaming:  2784 MiB, bytes=4133123 (per-region; +11% RSS vs FullBuffered)
#
# 3. The per-region path uses MORE peak RSS today, not less. Chunk 5 commit
#    explicitly documented this: "No memory reduction — chunk 5 alone cannot
#    drop buffers because the loop driver still returns whole-image-sized
#    quant_field / masking / mask1x1 / post-gaborish XYB that the butteraugli
#    loop and encode_from_precomputed expect."
#
# 4. The per-region path's bytes-level FP drift is small (4133123 vs 4131213 =
#    +0.046% bytes), well within the chunk-5-documented 0.1% worst-case
#    envelope. The test `rate_control_buffering_dispatch_routes_correctly`
#    pins this at <1%.
#
# 5. Bytes split into two equivalence classes confirms the chunk-6 dispatch
#    is correctly routing on Buffering value AT THE RATE-CONTROL PATH:
#    - whole-image class: FullBuffered, Threshold2048
#    - per-region class:  Auto (resolved to BufferedOutput), BufferedOutput,
#                         FullStreaming
#
# Chunk-7 plan (to deliver the 2-4x peak-RSS reduction the prompt targets):
#   The default LossyConfig::encode() path's encoder.rs:encode_inner must be
#   refactored to use the same compute_global_only + per-DC-group encode_dc_group
#   shape that the rate-control path now (partially) has. Specifically:
#   - Hoist XYB conversion into compute_global_only.
#   - Replace the inline precompute calls (xyb_x/y/b allocs, quant_field_float,
#     mask1x1, gaborish_inverse_maybe_adaptive, compute_cfl_map_with_budget,
#     compute_ac_strategy_for_tiles) with the per-DC-group helpers from
#     chunk 3 (compute_dc_group) and chunk 5 (fill_dc_group_state_per_region).
#   - Replace the inline emit (parallel_map_result over encode_dc_group_section /
#     encode_ac_group_section) with the chunk-4 encode_dc_group primitive.
#   - Drop each DC-group's plane slice on global as soon as encode_dc_group
#     returns — this is the actual buffer drop that delivers the memory win.
#   - Mirror libjxl's `OutputProcessor::Seek` for the FullStreaming path:
#     reserve DC-global placeholder, emit per-DC-group sections to the
#     WritableSeek sink as they finish, seek back to write the real DC-global
#     + permuted TOC. Wire `permuted_toc=1` explicit-write for that path
#     (libjxl 6553831 fix).
